tion":"1787300385532048001-d0fa2fbd-7e06-4f81-9876-d3ddcdef6f86"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a36fa32cad6ff6d1b429087a084265c46a74d0fc51fb2dda5fd55a94a0a9321e","event_uuid":"53555aa7-6c5a-4f8e-9c9b-eb5ac8f75f93","position":{"commit_sha":"a0c28c6eeea278094ed2906bfdd7914edd8c5d41","position":"1787300394417126001-53555aa7-6c5a-4f8e-9c9b-eb5ac8f75f93"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"681b16cb059066dc83c1202199c1c8a223bbfa3fc4f565cc5e19c61c8a0379fc","event_uuid":"4a252b46-da76-4fd2-a867-1e0cbf628acf","position":{"commit_sha":"9cbda6a572e7fe0e2bb9558146a0c478a2abf2d7","position":"1787300827873128001-4a252b46-da76-4fd2-a867-1e0cbf628acf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"41c21410173986fc5ed5cf1fc4fbdaa895514ea370b022313ef8746899f5278c","event_uuid":"ae133a42-cfe7-4ccf-97f4-2a1870f27b24","position":{"commit_sha":"4e71dd78cf6ea11363efe85628b729510d76fcfe","position":"1787300837420736001-ae133a42-cfe7-4ccf-97f4-2a1870f27b24"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9deb56ab12a990654b1ea68ff43bd34b707e5758f229c0839c8613d6852ff3d1","event_uuid":"5fbb425e-d891-4cd5-9b76-f69918a1f270","position":{"commit_sha":"f9a7cd993e26917b8d6d9b553becf4c58ef4cf8e","position":"1787300842235436001-5fbb425e-d891-4cd5-9b76-f69918a1f270"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"not_a_bug","close_reason":"Operator ruling: review-plan fast-failing on blocked is intended, enforced behaviour, documented at AGENTS.md:128-131 with its rationale at :123-127 (a review pins its dependencies' material, so reviewing a blocked ticket certifies against material that can still change). The refusal is the mechanism working; --force is the documented operator lever. The ticket's premise — that a sibling widening of claim made the refusal obsolete — inverts the dependency: the documented invariant is the fixed point.","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Not a bug — the fast-fail on `blocked` is intended, enforced behaviour\n\nOperator ruling: review-plan fast-failing on a blocked ticket is **intended**, not a defect.\n\nCited authority, `AGENTS.md:128-131`:\n\n> This is partly **enforced**: `review-plan` on a ticket that is not yet claimable — status\n> `closed`/`idea`/`blocked`, or `open` but still blocked by an unclosed dependency —\n> **fast-fails with no LLM** (unsigned `INDETERMINATE`, exit 2) unless you pass `--force`;\n> close the prerequisites, then review.\n\nAnd the rationale it enforces, `AGENTS.md:123-127`:\n\n> **Plan-review in dependency order — never review a ticket and its dependencies in parallel.**\n> A review pins its direct dependencies' (children/prerequisites') material, so a dependency\n> changing after the review invalidates it.\n\nSo the refusal is the mechanism working: reviewing a blocked ticket would certify a plan against\nmaterial its unclosed blockers can still change, producing an attestation that is stale on arrival.\n`--force` is the documented lever, deliberately reserved for an operator's judgement call rather\nthan routine use.\n\n### The premise this ticket rests on\n\nIt argues the refusal's premise 'is now false' because a sibling change widened `claim` to accept a\n`blocked` source status. That inverts the dependency: **the documented design is the fixed point,\nand a change that collides with it is the thing to re-examine** — not the other way round.\n\nWhether `claim` should accept `blocked` at all is a live question I have referred back to the agent\nthat made that change, since the two behaviours have to agree and the review-plan side is settled.\nResolving it there is the right place; it is not resolved by relaxing an enforced invariant here.\n\n### What survives\n\nNothing that warrants code change under this ticket. If a gated `task`/`story`/`epic` genuinely\nneeds to refresh an attestation while blocked, the sanctioned answer per AGENTS.md is to **close the\nprerequisites first** — which is also what makes the resulting attestation meaningful.\n\nClosing `not_a_bug`. Filed in good faith off a real observation; the observation is just a\nconsequence of the design rather than a violation of it.","timestamp":1787300827873128001}],"created_at":1787300385532048001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"53555aa7-6c5a-4f8e-9c9b-eb5ac8f75f93","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0449-cf75-bb4b-41fd"}],"description":"## Discovered from\nbug `conversant-cepivorous-mastiff` (0449-cf75-bb4b-41fd), which widened `claim` to accept a `blocked` source status.\n\n## Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/claimability.py` lists `blocked` in `_NOT_CLAIMABLE_STATUSES`, so `review-plan` on a blocked ticket fast-fails INDETERMINATE with the reason 'not claimable: status is \"blocked\", not \"open\"'. That premise is now false: `claim` accepts `blocked`.\n\nResidual gap: a gated `task`/`story`/`epic` sitting in `blocked` with a MISSING or STALE plan-review attestation cannot earn a fresh one — `claim` refuses on the gate, and `review-plan` refuses to run. `--force` is the only lever.\n\n## Why it was NOT fixed under the parent bug\nThe blocked fast-fail is **documented intended behavior** in three places — `AGENTS.md` L129, `docs/user-guide.md` L338, `docs/workflow-engine.md` L34-35 — so changing it is a plan-review gate design decision with a doc-contract change, not a defect repair.\n\n## Scope if taken\nRemove `blocked` from `_NOT_CLAIMABLE_STATUSES`, correct the reason string (it asserts 'not open'), and update the three docs. Keep `closed`/`idea` fast-failing.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ae133a42-cfe7-4ccf-97f4-2a1870f27b24","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"697e-3c66-abcd-40f3","ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-plan fast-fails on blocked, so a resumable blocked ticket cannot refresh a stale claim attestation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d0fa2fbd-7e06-4f81-9876-d3ddcdef6f86","53555aa7-6c5a-4f8e-9c9b-eb5ac8f75f93","4a252b46-da76-4fd2-a867-1e0cbf628acf","ae133a42-cfe7-4ccf-97f4-2a1870f27b24","5fbb425e-d891-4cd5-9b76-f69918a1f270"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787306094287255001,"uuid":"3ea29e4b-655e-4023-b2cd-2a45d37bdbad"}